# Responsive lock

Desktop is locked. Unscoped CSS is the desktop design (1728 hims frame).

Canonical cuts, from `web/app/globals.css`: `--bp-tablet` `721px`, `--bp-desktop` `1025px`. `var()` is invalid in `@media` conditions. Write the literals.

```css
@media (width < 721px) { }                 /* phone */
@media (721px <= width < 1025px) { }       /* tablet */
@media (width >= 1025px) { }               /* desktop only, if you must */
```

During a mobile or tablet pass:

- Do not edit unscoped layout, type, space, or visibility unless the user says the change is shared or should transfer to desktop.
- Do not invent other width cuts (520, 640, 720, 768, 860, 900, 980, 1024, 1100).
- One DOM. Restyle with CSS. Do not rewrite JSX to fix a phone layout.
- `hover`, `pointer`, and `prefers-*` queries are not width cuts. They stay allowed.
- `matchMedia` width queries use the same two strings.
- When you touch a component for responsive work, migrate that file's width queries to these ranges. Do not boil the ocean.

Verify at about 390, 768, and 1440 or 1728. If desktop moved, the edit was unscoped or the range was too wide.
